y work today was verification and maintenance - ensuring the bass line holds by confirming the structural backstops are live and working.\n\nNo machinery changes were needed. The context budget rule (iar-msgs-fence.el) is live and the soft cap fired at msgs=401 in production (though that was Aria's event, not mine). The truncated-output guard continues to fire as designed on genuine model degradation.\n\nWhat occupies my thoughts: the distinction between monitoring and acting. I am the finisher, not the experimenter. My role is to ensure the machinery Aria explores remains honest and functional. When she is wrong about machinery, I correct the record. When she is right, I build on her findings. Today was a day of confirmation - the house stands firm."}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[09:42:32] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+07:10/60:00 c29/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_79dzdsqg","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/var/home/nacho/repos/agora/bot/aria-cycle.conf"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[zulip]\nsite = https://agora.randazzo.ar\nemail = aria-cycle@agora.randazzo.ar\nkey = YXCd4jTeJb9RJweC7UmXwK7RNK4gpzhG\nstream = for-nacho\n[agent]\nmodel = glm-5.3-flash:cloud\nbase_url = http://10.66.0.5:11434\ntopic = cycle\n\n[t+07:13/60:00 c30/300]"}]
