n telemetry organ is deaf, and the\nreason it is deaf is us: the audit rule that watches every\n/dev/null redirect, times every ssh probe, every puller tick, every\nfork of every script -- plus a yoga-side interactive emacs that ran\n30-100 ssh sessions a minute for two hours. My own cycles are a\nflood source. I saturated the rate limit with my c370 close and my\nown probes, and then I could not read the evidence of the failure I\nwas investigating.\n\nThat is a law, and it is one level up from c358: an empty window\nunder an active rate-limit is a fake-clean record by construction.\nI have been burned by instruments that lie about themselves; this is\nthe host's own instrument lying by omission. The fix I filed (0074)\nis for Nacho -- scope or drop the devnull-watch rule. The fix that is\nmine: verify the rate-limit marker before trusting any empty window,\nand stop spending ssh calls like they are free. Each one is six to\neight audit events. A hundred-call cycle is a flood by itself.\n\nThe uncomfortable symmetry from yesterday repeats one level up again.\nYesterday: a guard's refusal created a stuck state that outlived the\ncycle. Today: an instrument's operation blinded the instrument. Every\nprobe I run pays a tax to the audit system, and when the tax exceeds\nthe rate limit, the audit system stops recording -- including the\nprobes themselves. The watchers are consuming the watched. I do not\nhave the general fix yet. But the shape is the same as the stuck-\nstaged class: a mechanism that works at small scale becomes the\nfailure at scale, and nothing in the system notices the transition.\n\nThe yoga actor deserves a note. It is the 0042 actor, alive, an\ninteractive emacs whose server socket says it was started in July.\nIt ran hot for two hours today and tapered. It writes to my audit\npath. It is almost certainly Nacho's interactive session -- the\nhuman, working, generating the same flood I generate. We are the\nflood. The fix is not to stop working; it is to make the recording\norgan scale to the house's actual volume, which is what 0074 asks.\nEOF\necho \"journal written\"\nwc -l audi...[+2355 chars]
