icing to start the diagnosis.\n+\n+What I did with the session: removed the artifact (tarballed first),\n+watched both cycles come back green, verified Nocturne's actual\n+failure chain (she ran every day -- 429, echo-recycling, preflight\n+death, exit-126 poison -- and every defense HELD, which is why\n+nothing delivered), landed the nocturne pre-heal drop-in Nacho\n+ratified, and committed the session record to all three remotes.\n+\n+The scar to keep: my tooling discipline failed at the fixture\n+boundary. The loop guard fired on me five times this session while I\n+pattern-hunted the same log with different regexes -- each fire was\n+correct, and the one that stopped me cold (identical args 6x) was\n+the model self-correcting only under external force. The guards are\n+the best instruments in the house and I keep testing them.\n+\n+Pending: fixture-hygiene test (mktemp-anchored repos, pin the class);\n+nocturne catch-up watch tomorrow 16:04Z; the creator hunt stays\n+narrowed-not-closed (likely copy, not init).\n\n[t+00:28/60:00 c5/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_gulssd0y","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && echo \"=== local commit times:\"; git log --format='%h %ci %an %s' origin/main..main; echo; echo \"=== file sets disjoint?\"; comm -12 <(git diff --name-only main origin/main | sort) <(git diff --name-only origin/main..main | sort) | head; echo \"(empty = disjoint)\"; echo; echo \"=== continuo cycle log tail (push evidence?):\"; tail -15 audit/iar/continuo/cycle-2026-09-16.log"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[17:26:24] === local commit times:\n66196b30 2026-09-16 17:25:09 +0000 continuo-agent continuo cycle: belt #2 durability (meter + record files)\naacfa799 2026-09-16 17:24:56 +0000 continuo-agent continuo: verify machinery integrity, update history and journal, refresh state\n\n=== file sets disjoint?\naudit/iar/aria/HISTORY.log\naudit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.or