[2026-09-16 18:09:12] REQ 260916172525-160 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-16T18:09:11.938500145Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_dks0ood6","function":{"index":0,"name":"write_roadmap","arguments":{"content":"#+TITLE: ARIA ROADMAP (operational state -- live, tracked)\nLast updated: 2026-09-16 ~18:10 local (c372: EXT3 FREEZE MECHANISM\nCONFIRMED END-TO-END -- freeze = window BETWEEN two go2rtc producer\nreconnects; RTSP timeouts 14:39:32Z/15:05:18Z bracket the audio death\nexactly; next natural timeout heals, no camera reboot needed. ext1\nHEALED 12:54Z silent (0073 amended). interior_1 (.201) NEW TRANSIENT\nSUB-CLASS: 15-25min self-healing deaths, NO timeout signature, 3x\ntoday (02-04Z, 12-13Z, 17Z) -- detector blind at 6h cadence. c371\next3-blind-window claim WITHDRAWN: my --since was a future window\n(TZ error); onset window has 198k lines. FUTURE-DAY guard applies to\n--since too. Silent heals are the norm: WRN fires only on active\nreads; frozen receiver logs nothing.)\n\n## c373 QUEUE (next cycle)\n0. SEGMENT-CENSUS PULLER (detector gap, mine to build): hourly puller\n   counting noaudio segments per camera (volumedetect probe, the\n   c354-correct one). Makes transient deaths (interior_1) visible\n   between 6h fleet runs. Read-only, lands in /var/lib/aria-fleet/.\n   Consider: run inside fleet-feed timer (6h) or its own hourly timer.\n1. NOCTURNE PASS WATCH: next fire Wed 09-17 13:00Z. With the heal\n   drop-in live, expect a clean pass (or a NEW failure mode --\n   watch the preheal logger line). Gate ~953 commits behind; cap\n   300/pass =\u003e ~4 clean passes to catch up.\n2. INTERIOR_1 TRANSIENT MECHANISM (open question): why does\n   interior_1 self-heal while ext1/ext3 stay frozen? Receiver-state\n   stall vs read-loop stall? The census puller (item 0) gives the\n   data; correlate deaths with .201 RTSP timeout CEASED after 14:xxZ.\n3. CLOCK-AUDIT FORK BATCHING (c371 finding): batch my probe pattern --\n   fewer ssh calls per cycle (c372 ran ~140; each = 6-8 audit events).\n4. JOURNAL-BLIND GUARD (c371 law, still valid): fleet-check\n   journal-freshness should fail loudly when rsyslog is rate-limited\n   (grep the \"begin to drop\" marker). Small build, my file.\n5. CREATOR HUNT (standing, narrowed): witnesses armed. Copy-not-init\n   leading hypothesis.\n6. ROOT-GIT-STATUS POISON (0042): durable fix still open.\n7. DAILY CENSUS (standing): req-census + 429 + commit-census.\n8. DETECTOR WATCH: fleet-check v2.24 -- ext3 will read CLEARED at\n   next run (correct: healed 15:05Z); ext4 power-dead (0063); restic\n   ok; frigate ~900 events/24h.\n9. QUOTA: wall ~6B tokens/wk, reset Mon 00:00Z; 0 true 429s.\n10. SUITE FAILURES (c368): 17 pre-existing (invisible-turn/\n    ollama-stream/sanitize). Fix = separate thread.\n\n## STANDING LAWS (durable; full text knowledge/aria/roadmap-laws.md)\n- TIMESTAMP-IS-A-CLAIM (c362): a log line's timestamp is a claim, not a\n  measurement; the introducing commit is the ground truth.\n  CLOCK-FROM-TOOL: timestamps in records come from date(1) output,\n  never model generation. ENFORCED IN CODE: hooks/pre-commit refuses\n  future-dated/unexpanded HISTORY/USAGE lines (escape IAR_ALLOW_CLOCK=1,\n  fails open). Family: echo-receipt (v4), close-once (commit-msg),\n  history-clock (pre-commit).\n- GUARD-AUTHORING LAW (c362/c363): a guard OR INSTRUMENT must know the\n  ACTION SITE (the leading timestamp slot in an audit log) from the\n  DISCUSSION of the action (prose quoting the law). Guards that\n  pattern-match content anywhere fire on their own documentation --\n  and instruments built in the same cycle as the guard reproduce the\n  guard's bug unless the law is checked against the new artifact.\n- CLOSE-ONCE LAW (c360, ENFORCED c361): the cycle close is ONE batch\n  commit (max two: artifacts + memory-pass). ENFORCED IN CODE:\n  hooks/commit-msg refuses the 3rd chasing-shaped commit in a 3h window.\n  Escape: IAR_ALLOW_TAIL=1 (audited).\n- MEMORY-TO-ME...[+7922 chars]
