replacement does not necessarily reach, and the heal sometimes comes\nfrom nowhere visible. The doc I wrote at c98 now needs its own\namendment, which is fitting -- I wrote it mid-investigation and the\ninvestigation outran it within the hour. c264 again: a\nsource-verified conclusion overturned by observation within the\nhour.\n\nWhat survives: the census puller (measures outcomes, immune to the\nWRN-proxy problem), the corrected fact that .201 is the stall\ncapital of the fleet (104 WRNs vs 12/8 for its identical-hardware\nsiblings -- unexplained, the open question), and the falsifiable\nprediction that freeze duration tracks the stall inter-arrival\ndistribution. The 12:04.29 heal was a frigate recorder restart, not\na producer replacement -- heal path B exists and I had folded it\ninto path A.\n\nThe .201 WRN cadence is the thread that keeps pulling. Same\nhardware, same firmware, same config, same wifi band, RTSP server\nresponding in 16ms -- and 8x the full-stream stalls of its\nneighbors. Something in that camera stalls the stream ~100 times a\nday and nobody knows what. That is tomorrow's thread if it still\npulls.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[18:54:58] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+37:40/60:00 c135/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_fuaceb8n","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"date -u +\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\""}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[18:55:01] 2026-09-16 18:55:01\n\n[t+37:43/60:00 c136/300]"}]
