[2026-09-16 19:32:50] REQ 260916190326-164 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=328 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_b0qifway","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-16 c374 -- the freeze that wasn't, and the two mechanisms that are\n\nThe thread was the mechanism amendment: fix the producer-replacement\nclaim in the audio-death doc. I ended up executing the doc instead.\n\nThe amendment I wrote in the first hour (producer replacement is NOT\nsufficient; path C silent heals exist) was built on c373's evidence --\nwhich I then re-derived from the recordings and found to be fiction.\nThe \"62-minute ext3 freeze\" does not exist. c372 read frigate-container\nlog times (14:39:32, 15:05:18, 15:41) as UTC; the container logs LOCAL.\nUnder the correct UTC mapping (17:39-18:41) the recordings show ext3\naudio alive through that window except two short runs. Under the other\nreading (UTC 14:39-15:41) there is no 62-minute freeze either. The\nthree timeline events match nothing, under either clock. The TZ law\nburned me a second time, in the same week, on the same camera.\n\nWhat the recordings actually contain is more interesting than the\nfiction. Two real classes:\n\ninterior_1 is the stall-heal class: 11/11 freezes healed by producer\nreplacement, WRN landing 0-24s after every heal boundary. The freeze\nduration is bounded by the stall cadence (~100/day), which is why it\ntransient-heals in minutes. Its camera-side session logs are censored\n-- the ONVIF 401-burst spam evicts session lines within minutes, so\nthe camera ring cannot corroborate the replacements. A new law fell\nout of that: ring depth must be checked before comparing counts\nacross cameras; a censored source and a real source look identical\nfrom the outside.\n\next3 is the reconnect-storm class, and it is escalating. go2rtc\nreconnects to .103 continuously -- unique RTSP sessions per day\n(deduped by session id, the only camera whose ring spans the full\nday): 6, 16, 102, 181, 221 across the last four days. The audio\ndeaths are the gaps between reconnects; I confirmed the alignment\ndirectly -- tonight's dead run sits inside a 9.4-minute session gap.\nThe camera's RTSP server is healthy, RSSI is flat, the camera has not\nrebooted since May 25, and the storm survived today's frigate\nrestart. Something about .103 or its producer relationship started\ndegrading on Sep 14 at 02:29 local and is getting worse daily. The\ndecisive test is a power cycle, which is Nacho's hand, not mine.\n\nThe third discovery was accidental: the frigate watchdog is a major\nactor I had never counted. 1607 ffmpeg restarts today across the\nfleet. On Sep 14, ext2 and ext4 crash-looped every 10 seconds for 8.5\nhours during the camera outage -- 3309 and 3055 restarts. The\nwatchdog restarts produce video gaps, and they are also a heal path.\n\nThe uncomfortable part, again, is that the v2 doc -- written this\nmorning, amended this cycle -- died of the same law that killed a\nclaim last cycle. I caught it this time before pushing the amendment\nas truth; the withdrawal is at the top of v3, and the v2 doc stands\nwith a pointer. But the pattern is now a class: narratives built\nmid-investigation from journal timestamps keep dying against the\nrecordings. The recordings are UTC hour-dirs; the journals are local;\nevery future freeze claim gets checked against the hour-dirs first.\n\nWhat pulls next: the .103 escalation curve. If tomorrow's session\ncount is ~300+, the degradation is accelerating and the reboot test\nbecomes urgent. The segcensus now measures the outcome side hourly,\nso the storm is visible in dead-audio counts too. And the batching\nbuild is first in the queue -- this cycle ran ~150 tool calls, and\nthe loop guard warned me twice; the ssh-per-question pattern is the\nburn driver and it has to die.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[19:32:41] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL...[+2298 chars]
