d output=%d total=%d model=%s\\n\"\n323-                             (format-time-string \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\")\n324-                             (plist-get totals :requests)\n325-                             (plist-get totals :input-tokens)\n326-                             (plist-get totals :output-tokens)\n327-                             (plist-get totals :total-tokens)\n328-                             (plist-get totals :model))))\n329-          ;; c262 dedupe guard: belt#2 (iar--usage-write-log-now) and the\n330-          ;; kill-emacs-hook both call this function with the SAME\n331-          ;; timestamp+counts within one close. The second append used to\n332-          ;; land as an unstaged duplicate that the next belt commit's\n333-          ;; `git add -f' swept into history (the USAGE.log doubling\n334-          ;; census, c258-c259; root cause c262: reset_worktree resets\n335-          ;; REPO_DIR (i.ar), never the personalization tree, so the dup\n336-          ;; was never wiped). Guard: if the file's last line is already\n337-          ;; identical, skip the append -- the dup dies at birth.\n338-          (if (string-equal (substring line 0 -1) ; strip the trailing newline for comparison\n339-                            (iar--usage-last-line log-path))\n340-              nil                        ; duplicate: skipped, honest no-op\n341-            (append-to-file line nil log-path)\n342-            t)))\n--\n774:(defun iar--usage-write-log-now ()\n775-  \"Write the usage line NOW (pre-exit), not at kill-emacs time.\n776-Called from the cycle/one-shot exit path BEFORE kill-emacs so the\n777-write lands while the cycle's own commit can still capture it.\n778-Idempotent with the kill-emacs-hook write: both append one line; the\n779-second is an exact duplicate with the SAME timestamp (the stamp is\n780-the usage-snapshot time, not the write time -- verified 2026-09-07:\n781-zero same-ts-different-content pairs in either hemisphere's log),\n\n[t+14:54/60